From 373e87c78b70d0e34baf54bf4869fe0f822310b5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Deniz Kokden <koekdendeniz@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 09:57:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 119/127] media: sprd: import contiguous DMA buffers and
 suspend idle VSP clients

Allow the decoder to write directly to linear minigbm NV12 buffers.
Pin imported DMA-BUFs, validate contiguous 32-bit DMA ranges, and release
imports with per-file generation IDs once the decoder drops DPB refs.
Reuse freed import slots without invalidating coherent buffer mappings.
Use the reservation-lock wrappers for attachment map and unmap.

Bound the slowest permitted vendor clock level through a module
parameter. Its default preserves the vendor ABI; a policy value of zero
permits the measured 256 MHz path rather than the blob's 76.8 MHz default.
Apply changes only when a new CONFIG_FREQ request precedes a job.

Tie MM runtime power to ACQUIRE/RELEASE instead of the lifetime of every
open file. Revoke userspace MMIO PTEs before gating clocks and service
register faults only for the enabled engine owner. Inactive faults return
SIGBUS rather than touching an unclocked bus. Preserve the original high
CMA mmap offsets so MMIO invalidation does not remove buffer mappings.

On SM-T560 with Android clang r596125, verify ioctl rejection, timeout,
CMA/VMA lifetime, register revocation and reacquisition, H.264 High/B-frame
decode to Gralloc, import reuse and stale-ID rejection. A 120-frame Blender
sample matches the software decoder byte for byte. Suspend for 15 seconds
with an idle FD and both MMIO/CMA mappings retained, then reacquire and
verify the buffer and engine. Keep the existing audio overlay unchanged.

Assisted-by: GPT-6 (Codex)
